4. Presentation Output Exception

A Presentation Output is a completed presentation generated for particular
content. It may include the runtime player code, styles, and supporting
assets embedded by this Package for viewing that presentation.

You may view, host, copy, share, and deliver Presentation Outputs as part
of your personal or organizational communications, including reports,
proposals, training, and presentations delivered to customers. You may
edit the output to revise its content or presentation behavior. The
presence of the embedded player does not by itself prohibit this sharing.
Recipients may view and redistribute that completed presentation with its
embedded runtime and retained notices for the same presentation purposes.

This exception does not authorize extracting the embedded runtime or
templates to redistribute them as a tool, offering the generation service
described in section 3, or distributing the Package under the label of a
presentation output. Those activities remain governed by sections 2 and 3.
Rights in input content and third-party assets must be obtained separately.

